cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference Deliberation Room, please cite it as below."

title: "Deliberation Room: A Cognition-Preserving Interaction Architecture for AI Systems"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "McKinney"
    given-names: "Brooke"

abstract: >-
  Deliberation Room is an exploratory interaction architecture and research
  specification for AI systems that optimize for what the human should be
  able to do next rather than only what the model should say next. The
  architecture models cognitive state, person-specific reasoning patterns,
  linguistic and sociolinguistic meaning, and interactional context to
  support adaptive next-move selection while preserving human cognitive
  agency. The project also explores cognitive provenance, rhetorical
  transposition, data-minimized personalization, and domain-specific
  applications.

repository-code: "https://github.com/brookemckinney/deliberation-room"

url: "https://github.com/brookemckinney/deliberation-room"

license: MIT

keywords:
  - human-AI interaction
  - cognitive agency
  - cognitive provenance
  - deliberation
  - interaction architecture
  - next-move policy
  - human-centered AI
  - sociolinguistics
  - metacognition
  - AI-assisted learning
